    "body": "In this episode of Denatured, you’ll hear from Bruce Culleton, CEO at ProKidney and Demetri Maxim, CEO at Nephrogen. We discuss why kidney disease has long been a hard target for cell and gene therapies, and what new delivery strategies, therapeutic approaches and regulatory clarity mean for commercially viable products.\n> Listen on Spotify > Listen on Apple Podcasts > Listen on Amazon Music > Watch on YouTube\nIn this episode of Denatured, you’ll listen to Bruce Culleton, CEO at ProKidney and Demetri Maxim, CEO at Nephrogen. We explore why kidney disease has historically been a difficult target for cell and gene therapies, and how advances in delivery, therapeutic modalities and evolving regulatory frameworks are shaping the path to commercially viable treatments.\nHost\n⁠ Jennifer C. Smith-Parker , Director of Insights, BioSpace\nGuests\nBruce Culleton , CEO, ProKidney\nDemetri Maxim , CEO, Nephrogen\nDisclaimer: The views expressed in this discussion by guests are their own and do not represent those of their organizations.",
